        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): repair double-escaped JSON strings in tool call argument…",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\r\n\r\nclose #109478\r\n\r\nSome models (reproduced with ollama/qwen2.5:14b-instruct, reported cross-model)\r\noutput `\\\\n` (JSON literal backslash-n) instead of `\\n` (JSON-escaped newline)\r\nin code-like tool call argument values. After `JSON.parse`, the content string\r\ncontains literal `\\n` where real newlines were intended.\r\n\r\nPython code written via `write_file` / `edit` / `exec` tools is corrupted:\r\n```python\r\n# What the model should produce (after JSON.parse):\r\nclass Calculator:\r\n    def add(self, x, y):\r\n        return x + y\r\n\r\n# What actually ends up in the file (literal \\n and \\t):\r\nclass Calculator:\\n\\tdef add(self, x, y):\\n\\t\\treturn x + y\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe fingerprint is a colon followed by literal `\\n` then indent or consecutive\r\nescapes (`\\n\\t`) — Python block structure. The model double-escapes newlines\r\nin JSON, so `\\\\n` in the raw JSON becomes `\\n` (literal two chars) after\r\n`JSON.parse`.\r\n\r\n## Why This Change Was Made\r\n\r\nFour additions, all gated so normal values are unchanged:\r\n\r\n1. **Constrained decoder.** `repairDoubleEscapedCodeStrings()` detects\r\n   double-escaped JSON in code-like keys (`content`, `new_str`, `old_str`,\r\n   `command`, `text`, etc.) via the colon-then-`\\n` fingerprint. It replaces\r\n   only the `\\n`/`\\t`/`\\r` at structural code positions (after `:`, `;`, `}`,\r\n   another literal escape, or a real newline from a prior repair). Intentional\r\n   escape sequences in string literals (e.g. `r\"\\n\"` in regex patterns) are\r\n   preserved byte-for-byte.\r\n\r\n2. **Consecutive escape handling.** A secondary pass matches the first escape\r\n   in a consecutive chain (`\\n\\n`, `\\t\\t`) whose prefix is a regular code\r\n   character (e.g. the trailing `s` in `pass\\n\\n`). Once that escape is\r\n   replaced, the following one gets a real-newline prefix for Pass A. A final\r\n   cleanup pass catches any remaining escapes preceded by a real newline.\r\n\r\n3. **`command` key coverage.** The exec tool's `command` argument is included\r\n   via a separate `TOOLCALL_REPAIR_DOUBLE_ESCAPED_CODE_KEYS` constant so it\r\n   does not affect the existing smart-quote freeform key set.\r\n\r\n4. **Unconditional stream wrapper.** `wrapStreamResultRepairDoubleEscapedCodeStrings()`\r\n   is applied for all providers. Wraps both the stream delta path and the\r\n   final `stream.result()` path.\r\n\r\n## Evidence\r\n\r\n### Gateway verification (ollama/qwen2.5:14b-instruct, Windows)\r\n\r\nAgent prompted to write a Python Calculator class via `write_file` tool.\r\n\r\n**Before fix:**\r\n```\r\nPS> Get-Content calculator.py\r\nclass Calculator:\\n\\tdef add(self, x, y):\\n\\t\\treturn x + y\\n\\n\\tdef subtract(self, x, y):\\n\\t\\treturn x - y\r\n```\r\nLiteral `\\n` and `\\t` — file contains invalid Python.\r\n\r\n**After fix:**\r\n```python\r\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\r\n\r\nclass Calculator:\r\n    def __init__(self):\r\n        pass\r\n\r\n    def add(self, x: float, y: float) -> float:\r\n        \"\"\"Adds two numbers and returns the result.\"\"\"\r\n        return x + y\r\n\r\n    def subtract(self, x: float, y: float) -> float:\r\n        \"\"\"Subtracts one number from another and returns the result.\"\"\"\r\n        return x - y\r\n\r\n    def multiply(self, x: float, y: float) -> float:\r\n        \"\"\"Multiplies two numbers and returns the result.\"\"\"\r\n        return x * y\r\n\r\n    def divide(self, x: float, y: float) -> float:\r\n        \"\"\"Divides one number by another and returns the result.\"\"\"\r\n        if y == 0:\r\n            raise ValueError(\"Cannot divide by zero\")\r\n        return x / y\r\n```\r\n- ✅ Real newlines: True\r\n- ✅ No literal `\\n`: False\r\n- ✅ No literal `\\t`: False\r\n- ✅ Valid Python with correct indentation, docstrings, and type hints\r\n\r\n### Vitest (34 tests in repair suite, 273 total)\r\n\r\n```\r\n Test Files  4 passed (4)\r\n      Tests  272 passed (272)\r\n```\r\n\r\nNew regression coverage:\r\n- `repairs double-escaped \\n at colon-then-indent Python block boundaries`\r\n- `repairs double-escaped \\n in exec command arguments`\r\n- `preserves intentional literal \\n escapes in string literals`\r\n- `does not modify non-code keys like path or pattern`\r\n- `repairs consecutive \\n\\t structural indentation in code blocks`\r\n- `exposes repaired arguments on the final tool call result`\r\n- `preserves intentional colon-followed literal \\n in exec.command byte-for-byte`\r\n\r\nAll existing tool-call argument repair, decoding, and stream tests pass\r\nunchanged.\r\n\r\n### Safety: false-positive avoidance\r\n\r\nThe fingerprint `:\\s*\\\\n(?:\\s|\\\\[nrt])*\\S` only triggers on colon-then-\r\nbackslash-n followed by whitespace/escapes then code. Legitimate `\\n` usage\r\n(regex patterns like `re.compile(\"\\\\n\")`, documentation mentioning escape\r\nsequences) does not match because there is no colon preceding the `\\n`.\r\n\r\nThe replacement regex `/((?::|;|\\}|\\\\[nrt]|\\n)\\s*)\\\\([nrt])(?=...)/gs` only\r\nreplaces escapes at structural code positions, preserving intentional escapes\r\nin string literals byte-for-byte.\r\n\r\n### No sensitive data\r\n\r\nGateway verification used local ollama (127.0.0.1). No API keys, private\r\nendpoints, or credentials in logs.\r\n",
